  "adminSettingsRemove": "Видалити адміністратора",
  "@adminSettingsRemove": {
    "description": "Phase 21.6 — AdminSettingsScreen's terminal destructive row, below the hairline, OWNER-ONLY as of Phase 308. Phase 299 turned the endpoint into a HARD DELETE of the admin's user account — both this call and DELETE /salons/{salonId}/masters/{masterId} now hard-delete, so there is no surviving distinction between the two. The wording matches the approved design verbatim, and the confirm dialog body (adminSettingsRemoveDialogBody) is where the real consequence is spelled out."
  },
  "adminSettingsRemoveDialogTitle": "Видалити адміністратора?",
  "@adminSettingsRemoveDialogTitle": {
    "description": "Phase 21.6 — title of the destructive confirmation for removing an admin from the salon. Phase 308: the action is a hard account delete since backend Phase 299, not a salon-membership removal; only this description changed, the title verb was already right and stays."
  },
  "adminSettingsRemoveDialogBody": "Цю дію не можна скасувати:\n• акаунт {name} буде видалено — доступ зникне одразу;\n• адміністратор зникне з команди салону;\n• за потреби ви зможете запросити цю людину знову на ту саму пошту.",
  "@adminSettingsRemoveDialogBody": {
    "description": "Phase 308 — bulleted consequence body of the remove-admin confirmation, most-irreversible first (Phase 291 house shape). Backend Phase 299 turned DELETE /salons/{salonId}/admins/{userId} into a HARD DELETE of the admin's user account — it no longer nulls salon_id, and the pre-308 wording that promised only a loss of salon access was a factual under-warning. Deliberately THREE bullets, not four: an admin has no calendar, clients or reviews, so removeMasterDialogBody's booking-cancellation and history-under-a-saved-name bullets have no admin counterpart and MUST NOT be invented for symmetry. Bullet three is a guarantee, not a hedge — Phase 299 frees the email, so re-invite genuinely works.",
    "placeholders": {
      "name": {
        "type": "String",
        "example": "Олена Ковальчук"
      }
    }
  },
  "adminSettingsRemoveConfirmCta": "Видалити",
  "@adminSettingsRemoveConfirmCta": {
    "description": "Phase 21.6 — the destructive confirm button of the remove-admin dialog."
  },
  "adminSettingsRemoveSuccess": "Адміністратора видалено із салону.",
  "@adminSettingsRemoveSuccess": {
    "description": "Phase 308 — success snack after DELETE /salons/{salonId}/admins/{userId}. Says «видалено», not «вилучено»: backend Phase 299 hard-deletes the admin's user account, so the old «вилучено із салону» (reversible, unassign-only) wording became false. «із салону» stays — paired with «видалено» it reads as WHERE the deletion happened, not as a reversible membership change, and it keeps this snack byte-parallel in shape to removeMasterSuccess («Майстра видалено із салону.»)."
  },
  "adminSettingsRemoveErrorForbidden": "Не вдалося видалити цього адміністратора. Ви не можете видалити самого себе, і потрібні права власника цього салону.",
  "@adminSettingsRemoveErrorForbidden": {
    "description": "Phase 308 (D7) — 403 from DELETE /salons/{salonId}/admins/{userId}. Backend Phase 299 narrowed the caller to SALON_OWNER, so the old «потрібні права керування цим салоном» became wrong — an admin HAS management access and is still refused. Byte-parallel to removeMasterErrorForbidden. This is a backstop, not the primary defence: the staff_settings_screen canManageStaff gate (D3) should make it unreachable in practice, but the role can go stale between a cached staff read and the tap."
  },
  "adminSettingsRemoveErrorGeneric": "Не вдалося видалити адміністратора. Спробуйте ще раз.",
  "@adminSettingsRemoveErrorGeneric": {
    "description": "Phase 21.6 — fallback error snack for any non-403/409/404 failure of the remove-admin call."
  },
  "adminSettingsRemoveErrorConflict": "Цього адміністратора зараз не можна видалити — з ним пов'язані записи, де він виступає клієнтом.",
  "@adminSettingsRemoveErrorConflict": {
    "description": "Phase 308 — 409 from DELETE /salons/{salonId}/admins/{userId}, a failure mode backend Phase 299 introduced. Unlike removeMasterErrorConflict, which collapses three indistinguishable causes, this status has exactly ONE cause server-side (the admin's user row is also referenced as a client), so the copy names it instead of hedging. Before 308 this fell through to adminSettingsRemoveErrorGeneric and told the owner to retry an action that is deterministically refused."
  },
  "adminSettingsRemoveErrorNotFound": "Адміністратора не знайдено — можливо, його вже видалили.",
  "@adminSettingsRemoveErrorNotFound": {
    "description": "Phase 308 — 404 from DELETE /salons/{salonId}/admins/{userId}; the endpoint is idempotent by row absence, so a second DELETE lands here."
  },
  "adminSettingsManageSemanticLabel": "Керування адміністратором",
  "@adminSettingsManageSemanticLabel": {
    "description": "Phase 21.6 — screen-reader label for the trailing tune icon on SalonStaffProfileScreen that opens AdminSettingsScreen. Shown for an admin staff entry only."
